@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Model aliases — one vocabulary, four harness dialects

folder "Host" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "host env  or  host-side .env\nARCHITECT_MODEL · EDITOR_MODEL · SMALL_MODEL\nDARK_MODE · CODE_THEME" as SRC <<host>>
  component "cmd/proveo run\nforwards entrypoint.ConfigVars by value" as RUN <<app>>
}

node "Agent container" as CTR <<host>> {
  component "docker run -e ARCHITECT_MODEL=…" as ENVIN <<app>>
  component "def entrypoint bridge\n(in-shell, after prep)" as BRIDGE <<app>>

  component "opencode\nOPENCODE_MODEL\nOPENCODE_BUILD_MODEL\nOPENCODE_SMALL_MODEL" as OC <<app>>
  component "cecli\nCECLI_MODEL · CECLI_EDITOR_MODEL\nCECLI_WEAK_MODEL (+AIDER_* aliases)" as CE <<app>>
  component "claudecode\nANTHROPIC_MODEL\nANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL" as CC <<app>>
  component "cursor\nCURSOR_MODEL" as CU <<app>>
}

cloud "Ollama sidecar\n--local-model" as OLLAMA <<cloud>>

SRC ARROW_MAIN RUN
RUN ARROW_MAIN ENVIN : " ""-e NAME=value"" "
ENVIN ARROW_MAIN BRIDGE
BRIDGE ARROW_MAIN OC : " ""apply_env_bridges"" \n(normalize → ""provider/model"") "
BRIDGE ARROW_MAIN CE : bare id
BRIDGE ARROW_MAIN CC : bare id\n(strip ""provider/"" prefix)
BRIDGE ARROW_MAIN CU : bare id
OLLAMA ARROW_CLOUD ENVIN : overrides all three tiers\n(""-e"" applied after Env)

note right of RUN
  **Why by value, not via .env.**
  proxy/firewall **mask every dotenv file** under the
  mounted tree, and the ""input-output"" layout never
  mounts one — so the documented alias contract silently
  did nothing in the default egress mode. Forwarding
  them as non-secret ""-e"" pairs is the only path that
  survives every mode and layout.

  Secrets are never forwarded this way: they are
  declared manifest env, brokered, or withheld.
end note

note bottom of BRIDGE
  **Every bridge runs in the def's own shell**, because
  ""proveo-entrypoint prep"" cannot export into its parent
  (_spec/cmd/proveo-entrypoint/prep-process-boundary.puml).

  Precedence is uniform: an explicit tool-specific value
  already in the environment always wins, the alias only
  fills an empty slot, and ""--local-model"" wins over both.

  Tier mapping is **not** uniform — opencode's small slot
  prefers ""EDITOR_MODEL"" (falling back to ""SMALL_MODEL""),
  while cecli and claudecode map ""SMALL_MODEL"" directly.

  Each def then prints ""PROVEO_MODELS main=… small=…"" so
  the resolution is assertable from outside the container.
end note

note bottom of CU
  Vendor-pinned: no custom base URL, so ""--local-model""
  is rejected for cursor.
end note

note top of SRC
  **No two agents spell a model the same way**, which is
  why the aliases exist at all:
  * opencode — models.dev ids, provider-prefixed
    (""anthropic/claude-opus-5"")
  * cecli — litellm ids; local is ""ollama_chat/<model>"",
    and litellm also accepts two-level
    ""openrouter/<vendor>/<model>""
  * claudecode · cursor — **bare** vendor ids
  * OpenRouter dots its versions where the vendor dashes
    them; Vertex/Bedrock stamp a date (""@20251101"",
    ""-20250929"") and Bedrock prefixes ""anthropic.""

  ""proveo run"" sanity-checks a ""*_MODEL"" value against the
  ids it knows for the resolved provider and **warns, never
  rejects** — the list lags the vendors, so an unknown id
  is usually just newer than the binary. It normalizes the
  variants above before comparing, so a dated or dotted
  spelling is not mistaken for a typo. Silent when
  ""--local-model"" is set (the sidecar serves arbitrary ids)
  and for providers with no list.

  This catches the real failure it was written for: a
  mistyped tier propagates all the way into the container
  and 404s on every call with a vendor error that reads
  like an outage.
end note
@enduml
